ed to more than 300 fatalities and left thousands displaced. The commission will delve into the origins, escalation, and governmental responses to the turmoil. Initially scheduled to wrap up by November 2023, the inquiry has been extended multiple times to ensure a thorough examination of evidence.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/manipur-2023-violence-probe-commission-gets-7th-extension-report-due-by-may-20-2027/articleshow/135798276.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/manipur-2023-violence-probe-commission-gets-7th-extension-report-due-by-may-20-2027/articleshow/135798276.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T15:39:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135798425,imgsize-201298.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Priyanka Gandhi's suggestion accepted, Kerala to launch Honey Mission in Wayanad tribal village]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/priyanka-gandhis-suggestion-accepted-kerala-to-launch-honey-mission-in-wayanad-tribal-village/articleshow/135797704.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135797704.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/priyanka-gandhis-suggestion-accepted-kerala-to-launch-honey-mission-in-wayanad-tribal-village/articleshow/135797704.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/priyanka-gandhis-suggestion-accepted-kerala-to-launch-honey-mission-in-wayanad-tribal-village/articleshow/135797704.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T15:39:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135798448,imgsize-488732.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['No NCP merger talks': Maharashtra minister Bharne after meeting Sunetra Pawar]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-ncp-merger-talks-maharashtra-minister-bharne-after-meeting-sunetra-pawar/articleshow/135797411.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135797411.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-ncp-merger-talks-maharashtra-minister-bharne-after-meeting-sunetra-pawar/articleshow/135797411.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-ncp-merger-talks-maharashtra-minister-bharne-after-meeting-sunetra-pawar/articleshow/135797411.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T15:08:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135797636,imgsize-129962.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['My phone tapped': Rahul fires salvo at PM Modi; 'get head examined', says BJP]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/my-phone-tapped-rahul-gandhi-makes-big-charge-doubles-down-on-debate-challenge-to-pm-modi/articleshow/135796258.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135796258.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Rahul Gandhi accused PM Narendra Modi of having his phone tapped and renewed his challenge for a face-to-face debate. Samajwadi Party chief Akhilesh Yadav backed his allegation, saying technology could not be trusted in the age of AI. The BJP rejected the charge, with Kerala BJP chief Rajeev Chandrasekhar hitting back at the Congress leader.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/my-phone-tapped-rahul-gandhi-makes-big-charge-doubles-down-on-debate-challenge-to-pm-modi/articleshow/135796258.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/my-phone-tapped-rahul-gandhi-makes-big-charge-doubles-down-on-debate-challenge-to-pm-modi/articleshow/135796258.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T14:26:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135797874,imgsize-1227764.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Hopeful they will come': India on inviting Pakistan to SCO Civilisational Forum in Delhi]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/hopeful-they-will-come-india-on-inviting-pakistan-to-sco-civilisational-forum-in-delhi/articleshow/135795316.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135795316.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[India has invited Pakistan to participate in the inaugural SCO Civilisational Dialogue Forum in New Delhi. This event is scheduled to take place from November 20 to 22, featuring various participating countries. Union culture minister Gajendra Singh Shekhawat expressed hope that Pakistan would attend the forum. The discussions will focus on cultural ties and shared civilisational heritage among member states.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/hopeful-they-will-come-india-on-inviting-pakistan-to-sco-civilisational-forum-in-delhi/articleshow/135795316.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/hopeful-they-will-come-india-on-inviting-pakistan-to-sco-civilisational-forum-in-delhi/articleshow/135795316.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T13:55:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135795504,imgsize-108932.cms"/></item><item><title>